## name_length
discord: Give the rule a name of 1 to 100 characters.
plain:   Give the rule a name of 1 to 100 characters.
model:   [Fixed("Give the rule a name of 1 to 100 characters.")]

## description_length
discord: Keep the description to 500 characters or fewer.
plain:   Keep the description to 500 characters or fewer.
model:   [Fixed("Keep the description to 500 characters or fewer.")]

## reason_length
discord: Give the rule a reason of 1 to 1,000 characters.
plain:   Give the rule a reason of 1 to 1,000 characters.
model:   [Fixed("Give the rule a reason of 1 to 1,000 characters.")]

## counting_window
discord: Count cases from the last 1 to 36,500 days, or count every case.
plain:   Count cases from the last 1 to 36,500 days, or count every case.
model:   [Fixed("Count cases from the last 1 to 36,500 days, or count every case.")]

## too_many_fields
discord: A rule can have at most 10 context fields.
plain:   A rule can have at most 10 context fields.
model:   [Fixed("A rule can have at most 10 context fields.")]

## field_key
discord: Use 2 to 64 lowercase letters, digits, dashes, or underscores for the field name in the API, starting with a letter or digit.
plain:   Use 2 to 64 lowercase letters, digits, dashes, or underscores for the field name in the API, starting with a letter or digit.
model:   [Fixed("Use 2 to 64 lowercase letters, digits, dashes, or underscores for the field name in the API, starting with a letter or digit.")]

## field_key_duplicate
discord: Another field of this rule already uses this field name.
plain:   Another field of this rule already uses this field name.
model:   [Fixed("Another field of this rule already uses this field name.")]

## field_label_length
discord: Give the field a label of 1 to 100 characters.
plain:   Give the field a label of 1 to 100 characters.
model:   [Fixed("Give the field a label of 1 to 100 characters.")]

## level_count
discord: A rule needs 1 to 10 levels.
plain:   A rule needs 1 to 10 levels.
model:   [Fixed("A rule needs 1 to 10 levels.")]

## first_level_not_one
discord: The first level must start at a case count of 1.
plain:   The first level must start at a case count of 1.
model:   [Fixed("The first level must start at a case count of 1.")]

## level_case_count
discord: Start each later level at a case count from 2 to 1,000,000.
plain:   Start each later level at a case count from 2 to 1,000,000.
model:   [Fixed("Start each later level at a case count from 2 to 1,000,000.")]

## level_order
discord: Start each level at a higher case count than the level before it.
plain:   Start each level at a higher case count than the level before it.
model:   [Fixed("Start each level at a higher case count than the level before it.")]

## timeout_duration
discord: A timeout lasts from 1 second to 28 days.
plain:   A timeout lasts from 1 second to 28 days.
model:   [Fixed("A timeout lasts from 1 second to 28 days.")]

## ban_delete_window
discord: A ban can delete at most the last 7 days of messages.
plain:   A ban can delete at most the last 7 days of messages.
model:   [Fixed("A ban can delete at most the last 7 days of messages.")]
